    what: 'The two nerves of the sole. The tibial nerve divides behind the inner ankle into a medial and a lateral plantar nerve, which run forward between the muscle layers and end as digital nerves to the toes.',
    does: 'Work the small muscles of the sole and carry feeling from the sole and toes.',
    bug: 'A Morton\'s neuroma is not a tumour. It is a thickened digital nerve, usually between the third and fourth toes, squeezed between the metatarsal heads.',
